  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hoa Binh VFFC- social integration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhance opportunities for social integration of people with disabilities in Da Bac district and Mai Chau district, Hoa Binh province.
In this project, the Vietnam Fatherland Front Committee of Hoa Binh province plays the role The managing unit coordinates projectimplementation. ACDC, with 12 experiences in implementing projects and programs to support people with disabilities, Acting as project technical consultant. Specifically, ACDC sends technical consultants to participate and supervise project activities; Technical support in the process of developing, summarizing and reporting project activities as required by the sponsor. In addition, ACDC will provide and connect a team of relevant experts from the Central to localities such as the Ministry/Department of Labor, War Invalids and Social Affairs to participate in a consulting role for project activities.
The project is implemented with the goal of enhancing the social integration opportunities of people with disabilities with the participation ofthe community and relevant parties with the following intervention subjects:
Direct object: People with disabilities and their families can participate and benefit directly from project activities. Specifically, people with disabilities and their families can improve their understanding and benefit from initiatives and activities to promote social integration for people with disabilities and effectively implement policies to support people with disabilities according to regulations issued by the State and relevant ministries.
Indirect object: stakeholders involved in implementing policies/programs to support people with disabilities at the local level (especially the team involved in reviewing disability levels and implementing policies to support people with disabilities at commune and district levels); residential communities in project communes/districts of Hoa Binh province. These subjects have improved understanding of the role of social integration while promoting better social integration for people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
